// §14 entry 22 -- `u4:maior` (explicit byte order on a SUB-byte field) ->
// EXS-E0201 ("unexpected token").
//
// §5.2 "Bit-width fields", rule 3: "Byte order is required above 8 bits
// and is not part of the grammar AT OR BELOW IT. An unannotated multi-byte
// field in a `@transitus` type IS `:nativus` and is therefore already
// EXS-E0321; `u4:maior` does not parse, so it is EXS-E0201. Neither needs a
// new code." One code, not two.
//
// DEFERRED, FOUND BY RUNNING, CONTRARY TO THE PRIOR RECORD HERE. This
// fixture once read `status=run` on the strength of exsc's exit status and
// a `grep -qF '"code":"EXS-E0201"'` match against its diagnostics -- a
// PRESENCE check, not an exact one. Tightening tests/run.sh's shape=code
// check to require the exact SET of codes emitted to equal {expect-code}
// (a spec-guardian review's finding: a run that emits the expected code
// PLUS other codes still passed) found this entry was never really
// passing: run directly through `exsc aedifica --diagnostica json`,
// `u4:maior` now produces TWO diagnostics, not one --
//
//   {"code":"EXS-E0201",...,"message":"unexpected token",...,"snippet":":maior"}
//   {"code":"EXS-E0322",...,"message":"implicit padding in a @transitus type",...}
//
// -- confirmed by actually running it, not assumed. The first is exactly
// what this entry claims. The second is not: the wire-layout checker
// (entries 6/7/21's `EXS-E0322`) is evaluating `campus: u4` as if `:maior`
// were never there, over whatever the parser's recovery from the E0201
// leaves behind, and finding the same partial-trailing-byte violation
// entry 21 raises on purpose. §5.2 rule 3's own text says this should be
// impossible -- "Neither needs a new code" presumes ONE fires, not both --
// so this is a real cascading-diagnostic gap in parser-error recovery
// feeding a downstream checker pass a tree it should not still be looking
// at, not a defect in this fixture (contrast entry 19, whose fixture WAS
// the defect -- two missing `;`s -- and was fixed in place instead of
// deferred).
//
// tests/conformance/ is this agent's own tree; the parser and the
// @transitus layout checker are not (CLAUDE.md's Scope: "Do not edit
// another agent's tree; report the needed change instead"). Reported, not
// patched around: recovery from an EXS-E0201 unparseable bit-width
// annotation should not leave a shape the layout checker treats as valid
// input to evaluate.

@transitus
publica structura Malum2 {
    campus: u4:maior
}

// TEST: entry=22 shape=code expect-code=EXS-E0201 status=deferred needs=parser_error_recovery
